          <physDesc>
            <objectDesc form="codex">
              <supportDesc>
                <support>
                  <p>3 vellum leaves; 300 mm (height) by 190 mm (width, 230mm fol. 2
                    and 3).</p>
                  <p>There is a lacuna on fol. 2.</p>
                  <p>80 mm of the right edge on fol. 3 were cut off. 50 mm were taken
                    off the top of Fol. 2 and 3. were cut which led to missing text.
                    One piece, 40mm to 185mm, was taken from fol. 3 and added to the
                    bottom of fol. 1.</p>
                  <p>Sievers reattached the missing part that was glued to fol. 1, to
                    fol. 3. </p>
                  <p> Fol. 2 and 3 are missing roughly four lines at the top with
                    fol. 3 missing seven additional lines at the bottom, around 95 mm
                    (length). The missing lines on fol. 3 can be partly reconstructed
                    as there are bits of the lines visible. It is unclear which part
                    is missing at the top of fol. 2.</p>
                </support>
                <foliation>
                  <p>The manuscript is not paginated. The paragraph titles and column
                    titles are added on the site in red ink. In some cases, the
                    paragraph titles are separated on two lines at the side</p>
                  <p>Initials in black ink were added on fol. 1r. On the other pages,
                    space is left out for the initials to be added at a later
                    stage.</p>
                  <p>Writing mistakes were corrected, in some cases, the scribe added
                    the correction above or crossed out the wrong word. Accents were
                    added on some words, either indicating the syllable or
                    stress.</p>
                  <p>The book number is written in red ink on fol. 1. The paragraph
                    numbers are written in red ink at the side on fol. 1.
                    Additionally, there is a fading script visible on the bottom of
                    fol. 1v, presumably written in a different hand at a later stage
                    (possibly maria aere, aeve, hearts).</p>
                </foliation>
              </supportDesc>
            </objectDesc>
          </physDesc>
